# Interactive inputs

When the user must pick from a known set, call the host question control before any numbered list. Cursor uses the structured question UI. Claude uses the chat's interactive input. One option per choice. Multi-select only for code-sweep topics. A typed number, label, or option id still counts.

Number the choices only after that control is absent from the host or the call fails. Accept the number or the label.

Free text stays typed: a path, a line count, a commit message, a custom merge plan, or file paths.

An option label capitalizes the first letter of the first word. Every other letter is lowercase. **Cancel**, **Exit**, and **Return to previous menu** are last. **Abort merge** is just before that last item when the menu has one.

A plain **Yes** / **No** does not open `Agents/Rules/interactive-inputs/interactive-inputs.md`. Do not open that catalog when the choices are already in the skill, `options.md`, or git menu file for this task. Open it only for a hub menu whose options are not already in a file this prompt opened, then stop. Do not open that file on any other prompt.
